    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Enhancement of GABA-mediated synaptic inhibition is one of the mechanisms by which inhibition of central nervous system is controlled.   This appears to be achieved through a potentiation of postsynaptic GABA receptor activity. Among two types of  GABA receptors (GABA-A and GABA-B), GABA-A signaling enhancement has been found to be an important contributor to nervous system depression by several anesthetics   The aim of proposed research was to specify the effect of GABAA Antagonist furosemide on epileptic brain slice. For this objective, we use several in vitro epileptic conditions which accurately reflect the physiological ionic and pH changes associated with epileptic condition. We tested what change happened after introduction of furosemide and qualified the mechanism in which part of the brain this drug acted on and proposed the further aspects of use of anesthetics on epilepsy.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
